ject, because the verb ending shows who is speaking. Pan / Pani are the formal \"you\"."],"rows":[["I","ja","yah"],["you (informal)","ty","tih"],["he / she / it","on / ona / ono","on / OH-nah / OH-noh"],["we","my","mih"],["you all","wy","vih"],["they","oni / one","OH-nee / OH-neh"],["you (formal, m / f)","Pan / Pani","pahn / PAH-nee"]],"ex":[["I am a student","ja jestem studentem","yah YES-tem stoo-DEN-tem"],["you are tall","ty jesteś wysoki","tih YES-tesh vih-SOH-kee"],["she is my sister","ona jest moją siostrą","OH-nah yest MOH-yon SHOS-tron"],["we are friends","my jesteśmy przyjaciółmi","mih yes-TESH-mih pshih-yah-CHOOW-mee"],["they are teachers","oni są nauczycielami","OH-nee son nah-oo-chih-cheh-LAH-mee"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Masculine: add -y or -i (or -e). Feminine: -a → -y or -i. Neuter: -o → -a. Some are irregular, so learn the plural with the word."],"rows":[["masculine","dom → domy","DOH-mih"],["masculine (soft)","kot → koty","KOH-tih"],["feminine","książka → książki","KSHONSH-kee"],["neuter","okno → okna","OK-nah"],["person (masculine)","student → studenci","stoo-DEN-chee"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","dom, domy","dom DOH-mih"],["one book, books","książka, książki","KSHONSH-kah KSHONSH-kee"],["one window, windows","okno, okna","OK-noh OK-nah"],["one cat, cats","kot, koty","kot KOH-tih"],["one student, students","student, studenci","STOO-dent stoo-DEN-chee"]]},{"id":"by-to-be","title":"Być: to be","text":[],"rows":[["I am","jestem","YES-tem"],["you are","jesteś","YES-tesh"],["he / she is","jest","yest"],["we are","jesteśmy","yes-TESH-mih"],["you all are","jesteście","yes-TESH-cheh"],["they are","są","son"]],"ex":[["I am English","jestem Anglikiem","YES-tem ahn-GLEE-kyem"],["he is a doctor","on jest lekarzem","on yest leh-KAH-zhem"],["we are tired","jesteśmy zmęczeni","yes-TESH-mih zmen-CHEH-nee"],["are you from Warsaw?","jesteś z Warszawy?","YES-tesh z vahr-SHAH-vih"],["they are at home","są w domu","son v DOH-moo"]]},{"id":"mie-to-have","title":"Mieć: to have","text":[],"rows":[["I have","mam","mahm"],["you have","masz","mahsh"],["he / she has","ma","mah"],["we have","mamy","MAH-mih"],["you all have","macie","MAH-cheh"],["they have","mają","MAH-yon"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","mam brata","mahm BRAH-tah"],["she has two cats","ona ma dwa koty","OH-nah mah dvah KOH-tih"],["we have time","mamy czas","MAH-mih chahs"],["do you have a pen?","masz długopis?","mahsh dwoo-GOH-pees"],["they have a car","mają samochód","MAH-yon sah-MOH-hoot"]]},{"id":"regular-verbs-present-tense","title":"Regular verbs (present tense)","text":["Many verbs end in -ać or -ić. Pracować (to work):"],"rows":[["ja","pracuję","prah-TSOO-yeh"],["ty","pracujesz","prah-TSOO-yesh"],["on / ona","pracuje","prah-TSOO-yeh"],["my","pracujemy","prah-tsoo-YEH-mih"],["wy","pracujecie","prah-tsoo-YEH-cheh"],["oni","pracują","prah-TSOO-yon"]],"ex":[["I work in a bank","pracuję w banku","prah-TSOO-yeh v BAHN-koo"],["you live in Warsaw","mieszkasz w Warszawie","MYESH-kahsh v vahr-SHAH-vyeh"],["she reads a book","ona czyta książkę","OH-nah CHIH-tah KSHONSH-keh"],["we learn Polish","uczymy się polskiego","oo-CHIH-mih sheh pol-SKYEH-goh"],["they buy bread","kupują chleb","koo-POO-yon hlep"]]},{"id":"i-to-go","title":"Iść: to go","text":["To go by transport use jechać (jadę, jedziesz...). Iść is on foot."],"rows":[["I go","idę","EE-deh"],["you go","idziesz","EE-jesh"],["he / she goes","idzie","EE-jeh"],["we go","idziemy","ee-JEH-mih"],["they go","idą","EE-don"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","idę do szkoły","EE-deh doh SHKOH-wih"],["where are you going?","dokąd idziesz?","DOH-kont EE-jesh"],["we are going home","idziemy do domu","ee-JEH-mih doh DOH-moo"],["she is going shopping","idzie na zakupy","EE-jeh nah zah-KOO-pih"],["let's go!","chodźmy!","HOJ-mih"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["Order is flexible, but the usual order is subject, verb, object. Adjectives come before the noun and agree in gender and number."],"rows":[["subject + verb + object","Jem chleb.","yem hlep"],["adjective before noun","duży dom","DOO-zhih dom"],["add time or place","Pracuję tu dzisiaj.","prah-TSOO-yeh too JEE-shay"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","jem chleb","yem hlep"],["Anna reads a book","Anna czyta książkę","AHN-nah CHIH-tah KSHONSH-keh"],["we live in a big house","mieszkamy w dużym domu","myesh-KAH-mih v DOO-zhim DOH-moo"],["he works here today","on dzisiaj tu pracuje","on JEE-shay too prah-TSOO-yeh"],["the dog is black","pies jest czarny","pyes yest CHAR-nih"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put nie before the verb. Double negatives are normal: nic nie mam.","Put nie before the verb. Polish uses double negatives: nic nie mam. \"There is not\" = nie ma + genitive: nie ma czasu. The object of a negative verb often changes to the genitive (mam samochód → nie mam samochodu)."],"rows":[["not","nie + verb","nyeh"],["nothing","nic","neets"],["nobody","nikt","neekt"],["never","nigdy","NEEG-dih"],["nie + verb","nie mówię","nyeh MOO-vyeh"],["there is not","nie ma","nyeh mah"],["nothing","nic","neets"],["nobody","nikt","neekt"],["never","nigdy","NEEG-dih"]],"ex":[["I want","chcę","htseh"],["I do not want","nie chcę","nyeh htseh"],["I speak English","mówię po angielsku","MOO-vyeh poh ahn-GYEL-skoo"],["I do not speak English","nie mówię po angielsku","nyeh MOO-vyeh poh ahn-GYEL-skoo"],["I like it","lubię to","LOO-byeh toh"],["I do not like it","nie lubię tego","nyeh LOO-byeh TEH-goh"],["she is here","ona jest tutaj","OH-nah yest TOO-tay"],["she is not here","jej tu nie ma","yay too nyeh mah"],["I have a car","mam samochód","mahm sah-MOH-hoot"],["I do not have a car","nie mam samochodu","nyeh mahm sah-moh-HOH-doo"],["I understand","rozumiem","roh-ZOO-myem"],["I do not understand","nie rozumiem","nyeh roh-ZOO-myem"],["we are tired","jesteśmy zmęczeni","yes-TESH-mih zmen-CHEH-nee"],["we are not tired","nie jesteśmy zmęczeni","nyeh yes-TESH-mih zmen-CHEH-nee"],["he works on Sundays","pracuje w niedziele","prah-TSOO-yeh v nyeh-JEH-leh"],["he does not work on Sundays","nie pracuje w niedziele","nyeh prah-TSOO-yeh v nyeh-JEH-leh"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Yes or no question: start with czy, or just raise your voice."],"rows":[["statement","Mówisz po angielsku.","MOO-veesh poh ahn-GYEL-skoo"],["question with czy","Czy mówisz po angielsku?","chih MOO-veesh poh ahn-GYEL-skoo"],["rising voice","Mówisz po angielsku?","MOO-veesh poh ahn-GYEL-skoo"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","czy mówisz po angielsku?","chih MOO-veesh poh ahn-GYEL-skoo"],["is she a doctor?","czy ona jest lekarzem?","chih OH-nah yest leh-KAH-zhem"],["do you have a pen?","czy masz długopis?","chih mahsh dwoo-GOH-pees"],["are you tired?","czy jesteś zmęczony?","chih YES-tesh zmen-CHOH-nih"],["is it far?","czy to daleko?","chih toh dah-LEH-koh"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","co","tsoh"],["who","kto","ktoh"],["where","gdzie","gjeh"],["when","kiedy","KYEH-dih"],["why","dlaczego","dlah-CHEH-goh"],["how","jak","yahk"],["which","który","KTOO-rih"],["how much / how many","ile","EE-leh"]],"ex":[["what is this?","co to jest?","tsoh toh yest"],["who is she?","kim ona jest?","keem OH-nah yest"],["where do you live?","gdzie mieszkasz?","gjeh MYESH-kahsh"],["when is the exam?","kiedy jest egzamin?","KYEH-dih yest eg-ZAH-meen"],["why are you late?","dlaczego jesteś spóźniony?","dlah-CHEH-goh YES-tesh spooz-NYOH-nih"],["how much is it?","ile to kosztuje?","EE-leh toh kosh-TOO-yeh"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":[],"rows":[["my","mój / moja / moje","mooy / MOH-yah / MOH-yeh"],["your (informal)","twój / twoja / twoje","tfooy / TFOH-yah / TFOH-yeh"],["his / her","jego / jej","YEH-goh / yay"],["our","nasz / nasza / nasze","nahsh / NAH-shah / NAH-sheh"],["your (plural)","wasz / wasza / wasze","vahsh / VAH-shah / VAH-sheh"],["their","ich","eeh"]],"ex":[["my house","mój dom","mooy dom"],["your friends","twoi przyjaciele","TFOH-ee pshih-yah-CHEH-leh"],["his sister","jego siostra","YEH-goh SHOS-trah"],["our teacher","nasz nauczyciel","nahsh nah-oo-CHIH-chel"],["my mother","moja matka","MOH-yah MAHT-kah"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["ty / twój for friends. Pan / Pani for strangers, with the verb in the 3rd person (he / she form). Add \"Pan\" or \"Pani\" + name or title."],"rows":[["you, informal","ty","tih"],["you, formal (m)","Pan","pahn"],["you, formal (f)","Pani","PAH-nee"],["Mr","Pan + surname","pahn"],["Mrs / Ms","Pani + surname","PAH-nee"]],"ex":[["you speak (informal)","ty mówisz","tih MOO-veesh"],["you speak (formal, to a man)","Pan mówi","pahn MOO-vee"],["how are you? (informal)","jak się masz?","yahk sheh mahsh"],["how are you? (formal, to a woman)","jak się Pani ma?","yahk sheh PAH-nee mah"],["thank you, Mr Nowak","dziękuję, Panie Nowak","jen-KOO-yeh PAH-nyeh NOH-vahk"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: verb stem + -ł + person ending (masculine) or -ła (feminine). Future: będę + infinitive."],"rows":[["I worked (m)","pracowałem","prah-tsoh-VAH-wem"],["I worked (f)","pracowałam","prah-tsoh-VAH-wahm"],["you worked (m)","pracowałeś","prah-tsoh-VAH-wesh"],["I will work","będę pracować","BEN-deh prah-TSOH-vahch"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked (m)","wczoraj pracowałem","FCHOH-ray prah-tsoh-VAH-wem"],["she bought a book","kupiła książkę","koo-PEE-wah KSHONSH-keh"],["I went home (m)","poszedłem do domu","poh-SHED-wem doh DOH-moo"],["I will call you tomorrow","zadzwonię jutro","zahd-ZVOH-nyeh YOO-troh"],["we will eat at eight","zjemy o ósmej","ZYEH-mih oh OOS-may"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal (ty): often the stem or the stem + -j: czytaj! (read), chodź! (come). Plural (wy): -jcie / -cie. Formal: use proszę + infinitive. Negative: nie + the same form (nie czytaj!)."],"rows":[["read!","czytaj!","CHIH-tay"],["read! (plural)","czytajcie!","chih-TAY-cheh"],["do not read!","nie czytaj!","nyeh CHIH-tay"]],"ex":[["come here","chodź tutaj","hoj TOO-tay"],["do not come here","nie chodź tutaj","nyeh hoj TOO-tay"],["sit down","usiądź","OO-shonch"],["do not sit down","nie siadaj","nyeh SHAH-day"],["be quiet","bądź cicho","bonj CHEE-hoh"],["do not be late","nie spóźnij się","nyeh SPOOZH-neey sheh"],["open the door","otwórz drzwi","OT-voozh dzhvee"],["close the window","zamknij okno","ZAHM-kneey OK-noh"],["listen to me","posłuchaj mnie","poh-SWOO-hay mnyeh"],["do not worry","nie martw się","nyeh mahrtf sheh"],["speak slowly","mów powoli","moof poh-VOH-lee"],["wait a moment","poczekaj chwilę","poh-CHEH-kay HFEE-leh"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["móc (can), musieć (must), chcieć (want) + infinitive: mogę pływać, muszę iść, chcę jeść. Nie wolno = you must not; nie musisz = you do not have to."],"rows":[["I can","mogę","MOH-geh"],["I must","muszę","MOO-sheh"],["I want","chcę","htseh"]],"ex":[["I can swim","umiem pływać","OO-myem PLIH-vahch"],["I cannot swim","nie umiem pływać","nyeh OO-myem PLIH-vahch"],["can you help me?","możesz mi pomóc?","MOH-zhesh mee POH-moots"],["we must go","musimy iść","moo-SEE-mih eeshch"],["we must not go","nie wolno nam iść","nyeh VOHL-noh nahm eeshch"],["I want to eat","chcę jeść","htseh yeshch"],["I do not want to eat","nie chcę jeść","nyeh htseh yeshch"],["you can come","możesz przyjść","MOH-zhesh pshihshch"],["you cannot come","nie możesz przyjść","nyeh MOH-zhesh pshihshch"],["she wants to study","ona chce się uczyć","OH-nah htseh sheh OO-chihch"],["I must work today","muszę dziś pracować","MOO-sheh jeesh prah-TSOH-vahch"],["you must not run","nie wolno biegać","nyeh VOHL-noh BYEH-gahch"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["w = in; na = on / at; pod = under; obok = next to; blisko = near; o dziewiątej = at nine. After w and na the place takes the locative ending: w szkole, na stole."],"rows":[["in","w","v"],["on","na","nah"],["under","pod","pot"],["next to","obok","OH-bok"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","książka leży na stole","KSHONSH-kah LEH-zhih nah STOH-leh"],["the cat is under the table","kot jest pod stołem","kot yest pot STOH-wem"],["I am at school","jestem w szkole","YES-tem f SHKOH-leh"],["I am at home","jestem w domu","YES-tem v DOH-moo"],["the shop is next to the bank","sklep jest obok banku","sklep yest OH-bok BAHN-koo"],["the park is near the station","park jest blisko dworca","pahrk yest BLEE-skoh DVOR-tsah"],["we meet in the morning","spotykamy się rano","spoh-tih-KAH-mih sheh RAH-noh"],["the lesson is at nine","lekcja jest o dziewiątej","LEK-tsyah yest oh jeh-VYON-tay"],["the key is in the bag","klucz jest w torbie","klooch yest f TOR-byeh"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Add -szy / -ejszy to the adjective (większy = bigger); the most = naj- + comparative (największy). \"Than\" = niż: wyższy niż ja. Irregular: dobry, lepszy, najlepszy."],"rows":[["bigger","większy","VYENK-shih"],["the biggest","największy","nigh-VYENK-shih"],["than","niż","neezh"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","duży, większy, największy","DOO-zhih VYENK-shih nigh-VYENK-shih"],["small, smaller, the smallest","mały, mniejszy, najmniejszy","MAH-wih MNYAY-shih nigh-MNYAY-shih"],["this is better than that","to jest lepsze niż tamto","toh yest LEP-sheh neezh TAHM-toh"],["this is worse than that","to jest gorsze niż tamto","toh yest GOR-sheh neezh TAHM-toh"],["she is taller than me","ona jest wyższa ode mnie","OH-nah yest VIH-shah OH-deh mnyeh"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Taszkent jest większy niż Samarkanda","TAHSH-kent yest VYENK-shih neezh sah-mar-KAHN-dah"],["it is the cheapest","to jest najtańsze","toh yest nigh-TAHN-sheh"],["the same as","taki sam jak","TAH-kee sahm yahk"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Extra practice with the most useful patterns."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","on jest nauczycielem","on yest nah-oo-chih-CHEH-lem"],["you (plural) are students","wy jesteście studentami","vih yes-TESH-cheh stoo-den-TAH-mee"],["I am happy","jestem szczęśliwy","YES-tem shchen-SHLEE-vih"],["she is at school","ona jest w szkole","OH-nah yest f SHKOH-leh"],["you are my friend","jesteś moim przyjacielem","YES-tesh MOH-eem pshih-yah-CHEH-lem"],["it is cold","jest zimno","yest ZHEEM-noh"],["I study English","uczę się angielskiego","OO-cheh sheh ahn-GYEL-skyeh-goh"],["he teaches maths","on uczy matematyki","on OO-chih mah-teh-mah-TIH-kee"],["they work every day","pracują codziennie","prah-TSOO-yon tsoh-JEN-nyeh"],["is this your book?","czy to twoja książka?","chih toh TFOH-yah KSHONSH-kah"],["are they here?","czy oni są tutaj?","chih OH-nee son TOO-tay"],["do you like tea?","lubisz herbatę?","LOO-beesh her-BAH-teh"],["what time is it?","która jest godzina?","KTOO-rah yest goh-JEE-nah"],["whose book is this?","czyja to książka?","CHIH-yah toh KSHONSH-kah"],["how old are you?","ile masz lat?","EE-leh mahsh laht"],["how do you say it?","jak się to mówi?","yahk sheh toh MOO-vee"],["your book (formal)","Pana książka","PAH-nah KSHONSH-kah"],["their house","ich dom","eeh dom"],["my phone","mój telefon","mooy teh-LEH-fon"],["excuse me, sir","przepraszam Pana","psheh-PRAH-shahm PAH-nah"],["please sit down (formal)","proszę usiąść","PROH-sheh OO-shonshch"],["come here (informal)","chodź tutaj","hoj TOO-tay"],["yesterday I was tired","wczoraj byłem zmęczony","FCHOH-ray BIH-wem zmen-CHOH-nih"],["I will study tomorrow","jutro będę się uczyć","YOO-troh BEN-deh sheh OO-chihch"],["we went to the park","poszliśmy do parku","posh-LEESH-mih doh PAHR-koo"]]}],"name":"Polish","id":"pl","flag":"pl","note":""}